  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039, 0.7250) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder with multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The only major design axis not yet tested at these best-known settings is the RNA encoder type: pca_n2000 vs. scvi_n200. config_029 swaps only the RNA encoder to pca_n2000 while holding all other parameters at their empirically optimal values, making it a clean, direct comparison. Evidence from config_007 shows scgpt is clearly inferior (0.520), but pca_n2000 has not been tested in the multiprofile+vit_l+transformer regime; it could capture complementary variance or be more robust. This is the best use of experiment 9 because it either yields a new best for the final experiment or confirms scvi_n200 is optimal, reducing residual uncertainty. Expected cost is slightly lower than config_039 (~3.0–3.4 GPU hrs vs. 3.60) since PCA encoding is cheaper than training a scVI VAE, while the ViT-L image encoder and transformer aggregation dominate runtime."
}

